  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{7}{3-4\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$",
  "worked_solution": "The denominator is $3-4\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $3+4\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $3+4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{3-4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{7}{3-4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{3+4\\text{i}}{3+4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21+28\\text{i}}{9+12\\text{i}-12\\text{i}-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21+28\\text{i}}{9-16(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{21+28\\text{i}}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{21}{25}+\\frac{28}{25}\\text{i}=(\\frac{21}{25})+(\\frac{28}{25})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
